# requirements.in — human-editable dependency specs
#
# This file is the source of truth for CI and developer installs.
# It intentionally excludes torch, torchaudio, chatterbox-tts, and numpy,
# which live in requirements-ml.txt.
#
# WHY THE SPLIT:
# torch + torchaudio alone are 2–3 GB. Bundling them here means every CI
# container restores (or builds) a 3 GB venv even though the fast test suite
# (`pytest -m "not slow"`) does not perform any GPU inference. Tests that
# actually exercise TTS use pytest.importorskip("torch") so they are skipped
# gracefully when torch is absent, rather than failing with an ImportError.
# This file is processed by pip-compile (pip-tools) to produce requirements.txt,
# a fully-pinned lockfile. To regenerate after editing this file, run:
#
#   pip-compile requirements.in --output-file requirements.txt
#
# Do not edit requirements.txt by hand.

